NEWPAGE

 The dark cloud of war has fallen over the galaxy after many centuries of
 peace. The great central Empire, the Federation of Star Worlds, led by
 their great President Kirk, managed in the past to keep the peace between
 the empires of humanity by means of their great strength and Kirk's skill
 as a negotiator. Now Kirk is dead, killed by assasins sent by the malevolent
 Warlord of Cosmos. The galaxy has been thrown into war again, with violent
 factions trying to gain the upper hand, while the Federation seeks to restore
 the status quo under the leadership of lesser men. In the wings, two star 
 powers rise, with the goal of stopping the rise of Cosmos, and forstalling
 the other great powers' attempts to fill the vaccum left by the Federation's
 collapse. Though seperated by many sectors of space, these two powers must
 work together to secure their place in the Galaxy, and stop the drive of 
 Cosmos.
NEWPAGE

    THE POWERS OF THE GALAXY:
      FEDERATION: 
    The Central Empire, the Federation boasts of a strong starfleet and a
    strong centralized position, as well as numerous SRM fields in defense
    array. Their weakness is their reliance on jumpships, as well as the
    lack of agressive leadership.

      COSMOS:
    Possessing a powerful fleet of starships, as well as a driving will
    to use them makes Cosmos the force to reckon with. Backed by a vibrant
    industry based around two industrial complexes, Cosmos' production
    capacity is staggering. Their weakness is low technology, as well as
    the lack of a strong jump fleet threat. Slow moving, they nevertheless
    pack a mighty punch on arrival.
NEWPAGE

      SOLARIA:
    Once allies of the Federation, the Solarians have now severed ties with
    the Federation and embarked on a seperate policy of defense, coupled with
    a drive for the highest technology. Peaceful by nature, the Solarians
    despise war, but when attacked, fight with calm, thoughtful fanaticism.
    Their fleet is balanced, and the empire has a network of base planets
    and outposts which guard the tightly controlled perimeter of the empire.

      SAVIORS:
    Led by their religious guru, Bob, the Saviors aggressively persue their
    self-appointed task of bringing "salvation" to the rest of the galaxy. 
    Generally, this salvation is in the form of massive attacks by their
    well-drilled battle fleets. The first power to use Ninjas, the Saviors
    are fanatic in their drive for conquest, and brutal in their occupation.
    Their industry, however, is weak and disjointed, due to massive purges
    constantly occuring within the empire.
NEWPAGE

      DATAN:
    This strange empire, peopled by androids, and led by the mad genius
    Dr. Soong, is a dangerous element which seriously threatens the humans
    within the galaxy. Utilizing superior technology, the Datans have 
    fashioned several artificial mobile planets for themselves, which 
    they use to gain raw materials to build replacments for themselves.
    These planets roam the galaxy at will, and are very powerful. Their
    weakness is their capital, the sole planet in their empire. It is 
    rumoured to be hidden in an artificial nebula created by Soong.

      STAR GUARD:
    This powerful empire, possesing a large starship fleet, as well as
    numerous SRM fields, is (thankfully) defensive in nature. Settled by
    mercenaries from the ancient Garp-Romanic Wars, these people have a
    vibrant will to fight for the homes they have built. Ninja-like in
    skill, they will fight to the death before surrendering, prefering 
    death before dishonor. Their power lays in a secret industrial complex
    protected by a disruptor.

NEWPAGE
ENDTEXT

BEGINDESCRIPTION

WorldBackgroundIndex
