2:66 E:6	7	;Data Capital
2:67 E:7	8	;Star Guard Capital
EndIndex

TEXT 1
  Once the capital of the Tri-sun League, this planet was destroyed by
  the wave of Fanatics that swept the galaxy after the fall of the
  Loganians. Ruins dot the landscape, and the planet's two moons bear
  the scars of that long ago war of destruction.

ENDTEXT

TEXT 2
  This ocean world, called the "Mother of Seas" by its population, bears
  the capital of the Second Empire. Close to the Federation, it recieved
  favor from the Kirk before his untimely fall.

ENDTEXT

TEXT 3
  Earth, mother planet of humanity. Once lonely and forgotten, under the
  guidance of Kirk, new fame and glory were once more Earth's to claim.
  Now, after his death, the new rulers skulk within the walls of the
  High Palace and plan how to defeat Cosmos, if possible.

ENDTEXT

TEXT 4
  Called Acheron by its inhabitants, the capital of Cosmos is a forbidding
  place indeed. Hostile forms abound on the surface, and seas of boiling
  sulfuric acid cover almost half the planet. The home of a tough, cruel
  people, who brook no enemies, or friends, only slaves to their thirst
  for glory.
 
ENDTEXT

TEXT 5
  This desert world is home to the Solarians, worshipers of the Son God.
  While hot and waterless, the sands and heat have forged a people of great
  courage and honor. Alone in his Grand Castle, the Prefect of Solar tries
  to forstall his enemies, while maintaining his stringent code of honor.

ENDTEXT

TEXT 6
  A veritable Eden, this planet, home of the Savior and sight of his 
  numerous visions, boasts of almost perfect conditions. Called Yeshu
  by the pilgrims who flock here constantly, it is one of the most ill-
  run planets in the galaxy. Still, it is a vibrant center of commerce
  and trade, as long as you are "saved".

ENDTEXT

TEXT 7
  This artificial world, discovered by Dr. Noonian Soong, houses the mind/
  computer of the Datan empire. Huge banks of electro-fluid generators as 
  well as a giant hydrogen cooled super-conductor give the planet its power
  as well as fueling the obsessive mind of Soong, now trapped within the
  core of the planet.

ENDTEXT

TEXT 8
  Surrounding the girth of this gas giant are the glittering satelite cities
  of the Star Guard Empire. Protected by huge SRM fields, this capital is
  as well protected as any. Within the shells of plas-steel and titanium, 
  the people of this great empire attempt to forge a defence capable of
  withstanding the might of the other empires.

ENDTEXT

ENDDESCRIPTION

